        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e38cc13d1dd34e8ab332276a44b77cd2",
      "statement": "The router creates the job row before streaming the body and writes it to `jobs/<wiki_id>/upload<suffix>`; `ingestion.save_upload` consumes 1 MiB chunks from `_upload_chunks` and, once the running byte total exceeds `MAX_UPLOAD_MB * 1024 * 1024`, closes the handle, unlinks the partial file and raises IngestionError. Because the archive is stored rather than piped straight into the extractor, it is durable state that a later worker re-reads.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/wikis.py#L117-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:86a7e967e9de28c15415b16c8d4fd40b73ec52af135b53e2c4083b35847f3974:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/ingestion.py#L251-L264",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c24c4d90d79c8317cf66592de44b25cf9f888ab5575622e2491e68d55ec937aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/pipeline.py#L173-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30fcd12c3121c09e291efec4887f93b704d2a3deb8fdb4309638c06ba05b1664:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6865f3c1765944869e3b24ef065e8d42",
      "statement": "An over-limit upload leaves no orphan state: the router catches the IngestionError from `save_upload`, calls `store.delete(job[\"wiki_id\"])` (which removes the SQLite row and the whole `jobs/<wiki_id>/` directory), and only then answers 413 with the size-limit detail — so the client cannot follow up on the rejected upload and must send a smaller archive.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/storage.py#L219-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eec47ad246bc29d8b4aa9b806c08a1fcea6f52990ee2ba036e994cc56cd5ecad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/wikis.py#L125-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf8415c7263dab3c2a7b4726784b3ddeea3f78805318d629f4c2ab61cfb77f7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7dee5236d4e0451f80e1dae02a5fcda5",
      "statement": "`_check_member_path` is the path-traversal boundary for both containers: it normalizes backslashes to slashes, rejects names starting with `/`, rejects names matching `^[A-Za-z]:`, rejects any `..` component, and finally requires `(dest_root / name).resolve()` to be `dest_root.resolve()` itself or to have it among its `parents`; any failure raises `IngestionError(\"unsafe path in archive: ...\")`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/ingestion.py#L302-L311",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63f85c70b8223fed294137e87a344d4240066a989ce0c7bf1055dbbd5d390bf3:"
