    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc02acebc4944601988b115c7e292cb7",
      "statement": "Extraction is re-run only when the workspace is missing: `_fetch` short-circuits with \"repository workspace already present; resuming the generation\" when `repo_dir/.git` exists, otherwise it looks up `job_dir/<source.archive>` and raises `IngestionError(\"the uploaded archive is no longer available; submit the wiki again\")` if it is gone. So an upload stays resumable while the job directory survives, and once the archive disappears (lost volume, cleaned job dir, or `DELETE /wikis/{id}`) the retry fails and the wiki must be re-submitted — unlike a git source, which can be re-cloned from the token stored in the row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/storage.py#L219-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eec47ad246bc29d8b4aa9b806c08a1fcea6f52990ee2ba036e994cc56cd5ecad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/pipeline.py#L165-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26799b60be76fee1259142b49a458655383b804506620b1b0b1581afc3d1404f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c970f48f779442ea90153408a1bd91e7",
      "statement": "Uploaded sources never push: `run_pipeline` only calls `publisher.publish_wiki` when `source.get(\"type\") == \"git\"`, so every push-related branch (SSH/git:// rejection, token requirement) belongs exclusively to the JSON `POST /wikis` route.",
