    {
      "id": "claim_2bdb68be3940462fa0da9935aa8cb973",
      "statement": "The upload path fails at three structurally different stages, and only two of them produce HTTP errors: an unsupported suffix (or invalid `concurrency`/`mode`) yields 422 before any job row exists, an over-limit body yields 413 and destroys the row plus `jobs/<wiki_id>/`, and every archive-safety failure (unsafe member path, symlink/hardlink entry, `MAX_EXTRACTED_MB` overflow, missing archive) happens later in the worker and therefore surfaces asynchronously as a job completed with `status=\"failed\"` and the `IngestionError` text as `error`, never as an HTTP response to the uploader.",
      "evidence": [
